From: Rosen Penev <rosenp@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:53:47 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ag71xx: support the switch PHY on the first MAC

On the AR933x, AR934x, QCA953x and QCA956x, the first MAC can be
attached to PHY4 of the built-in switch, or with the PHY swap to PHY0,
instead of an external PHY. On the AR934x, the RGMII, MII and GMII bits
of ETH_CFG select the external interface of the first MAC, and the
OpenWrt device trees only set one of them on boards with an external
PHY. Boards describe the switch PHY as an MII PHY, so with qca,gmac the
driver would move the MAC to the MII pins.

Accept phy-mode "internal" on the first MAC of these SoCs, and clear the
interface bits for it on the AR934x.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Rosen Penev <rosenp@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/atheros/ag71xx.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/atheros/ag71xx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/atheros/ag71xx.c
@@ -1167,6 +1167,11 @@ static int ag71xx_phylink_setup(struct a
 		__set_bit(PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_SGMII,
 			  ag->phylink_config.supported_interfaces);
 
+	/* The SoCs with a switch PHY swap can attach PHY4 of the switch */
+	if (ag->dcfg->phy_swap && ag->mac_idx == 0)
+		__set_bit(PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_INTERNAL,
+			  ag->phylink_config.supported_interfaces);
+
 	if (ag71xx_is(ag, AR9340) && ag->mac_idx == 0)
 		__set_bit(PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_RMII,
 			  ag->phylink_config.supported_interfaces);
@@ -1872,13 +1877,14 @@ static void ag71xx_gmac_if_cfg(struct ag
 		if (ag->mac_idx != 0)
 			return;
 
+		/* None of them attaches GMAC0 to the switch PHY */
 		if (phy_interface_mode_is_rgmii(mode))
 			*val |= AR934X_ETH_CFG_RGMII_GMAC0;
 		else if (mode == PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_MII)
 			*val |= AR934X_ETH_CFG_MII_GMAC0;
 		else if (mode == PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_GMII)
 			*val |= AR934X_ETH_CFG_GMII_GMAC0;
-		else
+		else if (mode != PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_INTERNAL)
 			return;
 
 		*mask |= AR934X_ETH_CFG_RGMII_GMAC0 | AR934X_ETH_CFG_MII_GMAC0 |
